PATCH 580: the sky resampler 689a (an unpromoted mid-entry of 6877), the op-0x24 tail 82d0's table
base, and the byte width of the sky-block counters 3915/3916.

board:0002.  Read off the original's block trace (scratch/oracle/blktrace): the tile is built by op
0x08 (10e0 = 8df0 ; 3931 = 85d0 ; [0x3958] ; 6980) and op 0x24 is 8120 ; 9200 ; 82d0 -- the shim now
dispatches both that way (tools/native_main.c, same commit), and three things in the decompile stood
in the way:

  689a   `call [0x3958]` in 3931 lands on 0x689a once op 0x44 has set it (TCB+0xcc != 0): the sky
         resampler that fills the whole tile from the 5.SKY bitmap before 6980 overlays the terrain
         columns (asm 0x689a-0x6976).  Ghidra saw 6877 (the flat-fill variant) and left 689a a
         mid-entry with no function, so the port's icall trapped and the sky rows stayed whatever the
         buffer held.  Emitted here from the asm: 910c = -90e0 - (38ed/2)*esi, 9110 = 90dc>>3 -
         (38f1/2)*ebp with ebp = (90c0*90b0)>>16 << 3 and esi = (ebp0*90b4)>>16 (also 90bc); per row
         the sky row is (edx >> (32-[3916])) << ([3916]-3) past [3911], per pixel the column ebx >> 25.
  82d0   projects the target marker TCB+0xd2/0xd6 through the depth tables 395e builds at 0x4620 /
         0x4624 / 0x4224 -- Ghidra read the three as host addresses (never called until now).
  3915/3916  the sky block's row-count/shift bytes (asm 8d2b/8d32 movb, 8dcc/8dd2 incb, 6925 mov cl)
         were typed as dwords: `[0x3916] = 10` as a 4-byte store put 0 into the low word of the tile
         pointer [0x3918] (0x08324200 -> 0x08320000), so 689a/6980 built the tile 0x4200 bytes below its
         buffer and the top 60 rows of what 9200 sampled were the ramp buffer's tail (board:0023 class).

  Measured (AZER1, tools/oracle/samples/oracle_9200_framematched_pass08.*): at the matched camera
  (X=584132 Y=1142327, pitch 384, roll 256) the port's tile is 65536/65536 bytes identical to the
  oracle's, 9200's inputs (90d4/90d8/90b8/90bc, esi/ebp) and the DAC identical, the windshield 91.6%
  pixel-identical -- the rest is the original's HUD overlay (PL:1 UN:1, GOALS REMAINING, the reticle)
  and palette-swapped texel pairs.

